node_modules/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
.orchestra/

# agent worktrees (ephemeral, created by the Agent tool isolation)
.claude/worktrees/

# ── `.atlas/staging` is DATA that must never travel — `projection`/`cas` now MAY (TRAVEL-BY-REPROOF, task
#    #90 amended, owner-authorized 2026-08-18) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# THIS RULE USED TO DENY `projection`/`cas` TOO, and the amendment is deliberate, not a relaxation of the
# guard it replaces: a `seal:'proven'` fact now carries its OWN derivation (`witness`, #195) and
# `atlas verify-store` replays it through the sound oracle (#196), so a committed `projection`/`cas` no
# longer has to be TRUSTED — every fact it serves is RE-PROVED against the live index on every read
# (`read-access.ts`); trust moved from the committer to the oracle. `.atlas/staging.json` (ADR-0008) is
# different IN KIND, not degree: unratified LLM-proposed candidate material that never passed a door and
# carries no witness to replay, so there is nothing to re-prove it against — committing it is still
# committing raw, unauthenticated trust, and if it is committed anyway (`git add -f`) it is STILL flatly
# refused at read time, unchanged (`store-provenance.ts`).
# Deny-by-default, then re-include: `.atlas/*` ignores EVERY child (so a sidecar added later is ignored the
# day it appears, not the day someone remembers), and the negations below re-admit the files that are now
# trackable-by-design. Order matters — a negation must come AFTER the pattern it overrides. Note that
# `.atlas/` itself is deliberately NOT ignored: git cannot re-include a path under an excluded directory, so
# ignoring the directory would make the negations below unreachable.
.atlas/*
# `projection*.json` + `cas/**` — the re-provable half of the durable store (see above). `staging*.json` is
# NOT re-admitted here and stays denied by the blanket rule above — it is the one population this amendment
# deliberately leaves refused.
!.atlas/projection*.json
!.atlas/cas/
# …and the admin-owned policy, as before: the ratified config the doors READ, reviewable in the same place
# as the code.
!.atlas/policy.json

# runtime telemetry from the orchestrator harness — not product source
.maestro/
